/**
 * trakyo-docs-site — serves trakyo.io/docs: the static Zudoku build (dist/docs/,
 * matching basePath "/docs") plus worker.js for requests that match no file.
 *
 * NO `routes` HERE, ON PURPOSE. The route `trakyo.io/docs*` is attached to this
 * Worker once, outside wrangler (Cloudflare dashboard → Workers Routes, or the
 * API). wrangler only touches routes it is told about: with none listed it never
 * calls the routes API, so the route stays as it is. Listing it here would make
 * every deploy read and rewrite the zone's routes, which the deploy token (scoped
 * to this one Worker, Editor) is deliberately not allowed to do.
 *
 * Deployed by .github/workflows/deploy.yml. Never `wrangler deploy` by hand.
 *
 * Pull request previews: .github/workflows/preview.yml publishes each pull
 * request as a Cloudflare Preview of this Worker, at pr-<number>-trakyo-docs-site
 * on Trakyo's workers.dev address (workers.dev adds noindex). `preview_urls`
 * turns those addresses on and must stay true: every deploy applies it, and
 * false would switch previews off. `previews` is required by `wrangler preview`
 * and empty because the site has no bindings beyond its files.
 *
 * @see https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/ (assets + worker script)
 * @see https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/routing/ (html_handling / not_found_handling)
 * @see https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/authorization/workers/ (per-Worker tokens and routes)
 */
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "trakyo-docs-site",
  "main": "worker.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-03-24",
  "workers_dev": false,
  "preview_urls": true,
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "html_handling": "auto-trailing-slash",
    "not_found_handling": "404-page"
  },
  "previews": {}
}
